<div class="page">

<!-- HEADER -->
<div class="module-header">
  <div class="eyebrow">Key Challenge</div>
  <h1>Prioritization &amp; Roadmap</h1>
  <p class="def">Most teams don't fail because they chose the wrong technology. They fail because they chose the wrong problem, tried to do too many things at once, or never made a clear decision to stop when the evidence said to. This chapter walks through how to pick the right workflows, validate them quickly, and build a delivery plan that compounds over time.</p>
</div>

<!-- PHASE STRIP — 3 phases only, consistent colors -->
<div class="where-strip">
  <span class="where-label">Active at</span>
  <span class="phase-pip pip-engage">Engage</span>
  <span class="pip-sep">→</span>
  <span class="phase-pip pip-discover">Discover</span>
  <span class="pip-sep">→</span>
  <span class="phase-pip pip-execute">Execute</span>
</div>


<!-- ═══════════════════ ENGAGE ═══════════════════ -->
<div class="phase-section">
  <div class="phase-label">
    <span class="phase-tag tag-engage">Engage</span>
    <span class="phase-step-context">Step 2 · Business Process Mapping</span>
    <span class="challenge-pip">Prioritization &amp; Roadmap</span>
  </div>

  <h2>Use what you already know. Pick what you can actually win.</h2>

  <p class="prose">By the time you're ready to prioritize, Engage has given you two assets: a picture of your tech and data readiness — which tells you <strong>where AI can realistically make an impact</strong> — and a map of your business processes — which tells you <strong>where fixing something is actually worth money</strong>. Good prioritization matches those two pictures. Without both, you're either picking the exciting idea or the feasible one. Rarely the right one.</p>

  <p class="prose">The goal is a short, scored list of real candidates. For each one, you need two types of people: <strong>process SMEs</strong> who can tell you what the work actually costs and where it breaks, and <strong>tech SMEs</strong> who can tell you whether the data exists to support an AI intervention and how hard it would be to build. You can't score without both in the room.</p>

  <div class="sub-phase" style="margin-top:0;">
    <div class="sub-phase-label">
      <span class="sub-phase-number">How to score</span>
      <h3>Identifying processes, assigning value, assessing feasibility</h3>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p class="prose"><strong>Identify all candidate processes.</strong> Work with process SMEs to list every significant workflow in the domain. Don't filter yet. For each one, document: who does it, how many hours per week it consumes, what the error or rework rate looks like, and what downstream work it blocks or enables. You're building a raw inventory, not a ranked list.</p>

  <p class="prose"><strong>Assign opportunity value.</strong> For each process, estimate what it would be worth to transform it. Value comes in three forms: time saved (headcount hours freed up), cost reduced (direct budget impact, error rework eliminated), or revenue enabled (faster cycle times unlocking deals or outcomes). Your process SMEs give you the baseline numbers; your finance or EBM partner validates them. A rough estimate is fine at this stage — you're ranking candidates, not finalizing a business case.</p>

  <p class="prose"><strong>Assess technical feasibility.</strong> For each high-value candidate, bring in a tech SME to pressure-test it. Three questions: Is the data that an AI would need accessible and structured enough to use? Are there integration constraints or governance requirements that would significantly increase complexity? Could we build something meaningful in 90 days, or would we still be setting up infrastructure at Day 60? The answers determine whether a high-value process is buildable now, or whether it belongs in the "invest to unblock" category first.</p>

  <div class="artifact-section">
    <div class="artifact-section-label">Artifacts</div>
    <div class="artifact-grid">
      <div class="artifact-card">
        <div class="a-type">PPT · High priority</div>
        <div class="a-title">Current State Processes</div>
        <div class="a-desc">Captures the domain's people (personas) #, process/workflows, technology (current tools), data, operating model, and readiness baseline. The honest "where we are today" snapshot.</div>
        <div class="a-links"><span class="a-link" style="color: #8d8d8d; cursor: not-allowed; border-color: #c6c6c6; background: #f4f4f4; opacity: 0.6;">↗ Example coming soon</span><span class="a-link" style="color: #8d8d8d; cursor: not-allowed; border-color: #c6c6c6; background: #f4f4f4; opacity: 0.6;">↗ Template coming soon</span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="artifact-card">
        <div class="a-type">Template · Medium priority</div>
        <div class="a-title">Opportunity sizing</div>
        <div class="a-desc">Quantifies the value case tied to the balance sheet or G&A: baseline, target, investment, and ROI.</div>
        <div class="a-links"><span class="a-link" style="color: #8d8d8d; cursor: not-allowed; border-color: #c6c6c6; background: #f4f4f4; opacity: 0.6;">↗ Example coming soon</span><a class="a-link" href="https://ibm.box.com/s/vvzn7aozzmllmwb3dotjgcm2vy7e38ja" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">↗ Open template</a></div>
      </div>
      <div class="artifact-card">
        <div class="a-type">Visio · Medium priority</div>
        <div class="a-title">Business Process Map(s)</div>
        <div class="a-desc">Documents the current-state workflow: handoffs, systems, users, bottlenecks, and automation opportunities.</div>
        <div class="a-links"><span class="a-link" style="color: #8d8d8d; cursor: not-allowed; border-color: #c6c6c6; background: #f4f4f4; opacity: 0.6;">↗ Example coming soon</span><a class="a-link" href="https://ibm.box.com/s/5c43ream7jq8ezi0boiobmhslhpachwk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">↗ Open template</a></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- Prioritization matrix -->
  <div class="visual-wrap">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 580 288" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="min-width:340px;">
      <!-- axes -->
      <line x1="80" y1="258" x2="544" y2="258" stroke="#c6c6c6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <line x1="80" y1="258" x2="80" y2="28" stroke="#c6c6c6" stroke-width="1.5"/>
      <text x="312" y="280" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#525252">Feasibility →</text>
      <text x="40" y="143" text-anchor="middle" font-family="IBM Plex Sans,sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="#525252" transform="rotate(-90,40,143)">Value →</text>
      <!-- quadrants -->
      <rect x="80" y="28" width="228" height="115" fill="#fff1f1" opacity="0.65"/>
      <rect x="308" y="28" width="236" height="115" fill="#defbe6" opacity="0.65"/>
      <rect x="80" y="143" width="228" height="115" fill="#f4f4f4"/>
      <rect x="308" y="143" width="236" height="115" fill="#fdf4e3" opacity="0.8"/>
